device.notes:
The RuuviTag is an open BLE environmental sensor. Ruuvi publishes its advertisement formats and firmware, so this is a clean open target: passive BLE listen, no pairing, no cloud. Data is in the BLE Manufacturer Specific Data under company id 0x0499 (on-air little-endian 99 04); the format is discriminated by the first payload byte (0x05 = Data Format 5 / RAWv2, 0x03 = Data Format 3 / RAWv1).
DATA FORMAT 5 (RAWv2), 24-byte payload, multi-byte fields MSB-first:
  @0 format id 0x05
  @1-2 temperature s16 x0.005 C (invalid 0x8000)
  @3-4 humidity u16 x0.0025 % (invalid 0xFFFF)
  @5-6 pressure u16, 1 Pa with -50000 Pa offset (invalid 0xFFFF)
  @7-8/@9-10/@11-12 acceleration X/Y/Z s16, 1 mG (invalid 0x8000)
  @13-14 power info: upper 11 bits battery mV (+1600 offset), lower 5 bits TX
         power (2 dBm step, -40 offset)
  @15 movement counter u8 (invalid 0xFF)
  @16-17 measurement sequence u16 (invalid 0xFFFF)
  @18-23 MAC address

DATA FORMAT 3 (RAWv1), 14-byte legacy: @0 0x03; @1 humidity u8 x0.5 %; @2-3 temperature (MSB=sign, x0.01 C); @4-5 pressure (1 Pa, -50000 offset); @6-7/@8-9/@10-11 accel X/Y/Z mG; @12-13 battery mV.
